{
  "rationale": "This is iteration 0, so there is no Integration Feedback or Geometry Race Data yet. I am choosing a neutral baseline to give the Integrator a stable platform and a clean first measurement. Five sensors spaced 0.02 m apart at x = -0.04 to +0.04 cover about 0.09 m across the robot. With 12 mm footprints the sensors overlap the 25 mm tape at all times, so the line is seen even when the robot is off-centre. Placing the sensors 0.05 m ahead of the axle gives the controller lead time to react at speed. A 0.12 m wheel track and 0.03 m wheel radius keep turn authority moderate. A 0.8 kg mass and 0.12 m body width keep the off-track limit at its 0.06 m floor, which leaves room for early oscillation without ending the run. Expected result: a first race that completes the course with few line-loss events and a moderate RMS error, which will show whether the sensor spread is adequate. Hypotheses to test: (1) 5 sensors at 0.02 m spacing give smoother signals than 3; (2) a forward offset of 0.05 m improves tracking on bends; (3) the 0.12 m wheel track is enough for tight bends without excessive yaw inertia.",
  "geometry": {
    "sensor_positions": [
      {"x": -0.04, "y": 0.05},
      {"x": -0.02, "y": 0.05},
      {"x": 0.0, "y": 0.05},
      {"x": 0.02, "y": 0.05},
      {"x": 0.04, "y": 0.05}
    ],
    "sensor_size": 0.012,
    "wheel_track": 0.12,
    "wheel_radius": 0.03,
    "body_width": 0.12,
    "body_length": 0.18,
    "mass": 0.8
  },
  "intent": "Baseline symmetric five-sensor array with a 0.05 m forward offset, 12 mm footprints and 0.02 m spacing, so every sensor overlaps the 25 mm tape and the signal is well spread across the line. Body and wheel dimensions are moderate, keeping yaw inertia and off-track margin balanced. Expect a completed run with few line-loss events; if the Integrator reports oscillation or loss on sharp bends, the next revision should narrow the array or change the forward offset.",
  "feedback_request": {
    "questions": [
      "Did the five-sensor array give a usable, smooth signal with the chosen weights, or did any sensor saturate or dropout?",
      "Was the 0.05 m forward offset helpful or harmful on bends, and what happened at the sharpest bend?",
      "Was the 0.12 m wheel track and 0.8 kg mass enough for stable turning, or did the robot slide or oscillate?",
      "Did the robot ever approach the off-track limit, and at what speed?"
    ],
    "requested_changes_if_any": "Report which geometry field most limited controller tuning, e.g. sensor spacing, forward offset, or track width."
  },
  "learning": "No prior evidence. Baseline chosen to isolate the effect of sensor spread and forward offset in the first race.",
  "_presentation": {
    "entity0": {
      "label": "Baseline 5-sensor array",
      "notes": "A neutral first geometry: five 12 mm sensors at 0.02 m spacing, 0.05 m ahead of the axle, on a 0.12 m track and 0.8 kg body. No race evidence yet, so this is a baseline to test sensor spread and forward offset."
    }
  }
}
